.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH whittle 1  "whittle 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
whittle \- Coordinate\-consistent trimming of long\-read uBAM and tagged FASTQ
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwhittle\fR [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-input\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-preserve\-order\fR] [\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-min\-length\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-max\-length\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-min\-quality\fR] [\fB\-Q\fR|\fB\-\-max\-quality\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-min\-gc\fR] [\fB\-G\fR|\fB\-\-max\-gc\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-quality\-mode\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-trim\-front\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-trim\-tail\fR] [\fB\-\-trim\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-best\-quality\-segment\fR] [\fB\-\-split\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-split\-min\-low\-quality\-bases\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-signal\-tags\fR] [\fB\-\-trim\-barcodes\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-kinetics\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-search\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\-reads\fR] [\fB\-\-discover\-adapters\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Coordinate\-consistent trimming of long\-read uBAM and tagged FASTQ
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SETUP
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Input FASTQ\-family file, unaligned BAM, or directory; \- means stdin. Defaults to stdin
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Output file, whose extension selects the format; \- means stdout. Defaults to stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Force the input format instead of detecting it from the path or stream
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq: Plain FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz: gzip\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz: BGZF\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
bam: Unaligned BAM
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Force the output format instead of selecting it from the output path
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fastq: Plain FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-gz: gzip\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
fastq\-bgz: BGZF\-compressed FASTQ
.IP \(bu 2
bam: Unaligned BAM
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads, at least 1; values above the CPU count are clamped to it. Defaults to all detected CPUs
.TP
\fB\-\-preserve\-order\fR
Write records in input order when running with more than one thread. Without it, records are written as they finish, which is faster and uses less memory but is not reproducible between runs
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-compression\-level\fR \fI<0\-9>\fR
BGZF compression level (0\-9) for BAM, .bgz and .gz output. Lower levels are faster and produce larger files. Ignored for plain FASTQ. Defaults to 4 for .gz and 6 for .bgz and BAM
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\-json\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write a machine\-readable JSON run summary (counters plus the resolved settings) to this path. Written even under \-\-quiet
.SH TAGS
.TP
\fB\-\-fastq\-tags\fR \fI<all|none|TAGS>\fR [default: all]
Aux tags written into FASTQ headers on BAM or tagged FASTQ input: all, none, or a list such as MM,ML,RG
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-signal\-tags\fR
Keep ONT signal tags consistent through trimming (slice mv, update ts, ns, sp and pi) for signal\-aware tools such as Remora and Clair3 v2, instead of dropping them. BAM\-to\-BAM only; requires a DNA or RNA basecall_model in the read\-group description
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Remove this two\-character aux tag from every output record. Repeatable. BAM or tagged FASTQ input
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-kinetics\fR
Remove the per\-base kinetics and alignment\-count arrays (ip pw fi fp ri rp sa sm sx). BAM or tagged FASTQ input
.SH LOGGING
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase logging detail: \-v is debug, \-vv is trace (at most two). Overridden by WHITTLE_LOG
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Silence progress and info output; warnings and errors still print. Conflicts with \-v and \-\-progress
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting, independent of the log level: auto selects a bar on a terminal and periodic lines otherwise; bar and plain force one form; none disables progress and keeps the banner and summary. A bar falls back to lines under \-v or WHITTLE_LOG
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, periodic lines otherwise
.IP \(bu 2
bar: The animated bar, unless \-v or WHITTLE_LOG asks for log lines
.IP \(bu 2
plain: Always periodic lines, never a bar
.IP \(bu 2
none: No progress reporting; the banner and summary still print
.RE
.SH FILTERING
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-min\-length\fR \fI<BASES>\fR [default: 1]
Minimum post\-trim segment length
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-max\-length\fR \fI<BASES>\fR
Maximum post\-trim segment length
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-min\-quality\fR \fI<PHRED>\fR [default: 0]
Minimum post\-trim segment quality under \-\-quality\-mode
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-max\-quality\fR \fI<PHRED>\fR [default: 1000]
Maximum post\-trim segment quality under \-\-quality\-mode
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-min\-gc\fR \fI<FRACTION>\fR
Minimum post\-trim GC fraction (0 to 1; 0.4 means 40%)
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-max\-gc\fR \fI<FRACTION>\fR
Maximum post\-trim GC fraction (0 to 1; 0.4 means 40%)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-quality\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: mean]
Quality calculation used by \-\-min\-quality and \-\-max\-quality on each output segment. Does not affect trimming, best\-segment selection or splitting
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
mean: Mean error probability, expressed as a Phred score
.IP \(bu 2
arithmetic: Mean of the Phred scores
.IP \(bu 2
median: Median Phred score
.RE
.SH TRIMMING
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-trim\-front\fR \fI<BASES>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from each adapter\-derived segment\*(Aqs 5\*(Aq end, after barcode restriction and before quality processing. Applied once; quality\-split pieces are not cropped again
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-trim\-tail\fR \fI<BASES>\fR [default: 0]
Remove this many bases from each adapter\-derived segment\*(Aqs 3\*(Aq end, after barcode restriction and before quality processing. Applied once; quality\-split pieces are not cropped again
.TP
\fB\-\-trim\-quality\fR \fI<PHRED>\fR
Trim both ends until reaching a base at or above PHRED. Mutually exclusive with \-\-best\-quality\-segment and \-\-split\-quality
.TP
\fB\-\-best\-quality\-segment\fR \fI<PHRED>\fR
Keep the highest\-scoring segment using cumulative base\-error probabilities and the PHRED cutoff (modified Mott). May retain bases below the cutoff. Applied separately to each adapter\-derived segment
.TP
\fB\-\-split\-quality\fR \fI<PHRED>\fR
Split each cropped adapter\-derived segment at consecutive bases below PHRED. Number the final segments in original\-read order. \-\-split\-min\-low\-quality\-bases sets the minimum number required to split
.TP
\fB\-\-split\-min\-low\-quality\-bases\fR \fI<BASES>\fR
Minimum consecutive bases below \-\-split\-quality required to split. Shorter internal stretches are retained; low\-quality ends are trimmed. Requires \-\-split\-quality. Defaults to 1
.TP
\fB\-\-trim\-barcodes\fR
Restrict adapter\-derived segments to the retained interval recorded in the original bi aux tag, before fixed cropping. Requires BAM or tagged FASTQ; does not detect barcodes
.SH "ADAPTER TRIMMING"
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-adapter\-fasta\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Adapter FASTA; sequences may use IUPAC codes, and entries shorter than 11 bp are skipped. An entry whose header description contains the word primer or barcode is trimmed at read ends only; every other entry also splits reads at interior hits. Enables adapter trimming
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-preset\fR \fI<KITS>\fR
Built\-in kit presets, comma\-separated: lsk114, rad114 (ulk114), rbk114, nbd114, pcb114 (pcs114), rpb114, mab114, rna004, pacbio, ont (every ONT kit), all. Enables adapter trimming. Defaults to none
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-error\-rate\fR \fI<FRACTION>\fR
End\-match tolerance as a fraction of adapter length; interior splits use half. Requires an adapter source. Defaults to 0.2
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-end\-search\fR \fI<BASES>\fR
Bases at each read end searched for a terminal adapter. Requires an adapter source. Defaults to 150
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-ends\-only\fR
Trim adapters at read ends only; never split on interior adapters. Does not disable quality splitting
.TP
\fB\-\-adapter\-sample\-reads\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Reads inspected for preset presence or adapter discovery; at least 100. 0 disables presence detection and uses the full preset; discovery requires sampling. Ignored with \-\-adapter\-fasta unless discovering adapters. Defaults to 2000 with a preset and 40000 under \-\-discover\-adapters. Sampling is also bounded by 256 MiB of payload and 64 Mi bases
.TP
\fB\-\-discover\-adapters\fR [\fI<ACTION>\fR]
Discover adapters and primers de novo with automatic boundaries. Report prints discovered FASTA to stdout and exits without read output or a JSON summary. Both actions use the same sequences. Defaults to trim when given no value
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
trim: Trim reads with the inferred sequences
.IP \(bu 2
report: Print inferred FASTA to stdout and do not write read output
.RE
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  whittle \-i reads.fastq.gz \-o trimmed.fastq.gz \-H 20 \-T 20 \-\-trim\-quality 8 \-l 500 \-q 10 \-t 8
  whittle \-i reads.bam \-o trimmed.bam \-\-split\-quality 9 \-\-split\-min\-low\-quality\-bases 50 \-l 1000
  whittle \-i reads.bam \-o trimmed.bam \-\-adapter\-preset lsk114 \-l 500
  whittle \-i 16s.fastq.gz \-o trimmed.fastq.gz \-\-adapter\-preset mab114
  samtools fastq \-T MM,ML,MN reads.bam | whittle \-o trimmed.fastq.gz \-H 10 \-T 10
  whittle \-i reads.bam \-o reads.fastq.gz \-\-quiet \-\-summary\-json qc.json
